---
import BaseHead from "~/components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "~/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "~/components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "~/consts";
import Title from "~/components/Title.astro";
import "~/layouts/BlogPost.css";
const LAST_UPDATE = "October 16, 2026";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main class="BlogPost">
      <Title title="Privacy Policy" />
      <section class="prose">
        <h2>Last updated: {LAST_UPDATE}</h2>

        <p>
          At valerionarcisi.me, visitor privacy is a priority. The site sets no cookies for
          visitors, shows no advertising and loads no third-party tracking tools. Two articles
          may embed external content (a YouTube video and a Relive widget), but it loads only
          after you click: see section 3.
        </p>

        <hr />
        <h2>1. Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use a self-hosted analytics system with no cookies and no third-party tools. We
          never store your IP address. It is used only in memory, together with your browser,
          to compute a pseudonymous identifier with a secret key that changes every day: the
          key is deleted after two days, and from then on it is no longer possible to trace a
          person or link their visits. In the meantime, the pages seen by the same visitor
          may be grouped into one visit (as long as they are no more than 30 minutes apart) to
          understand how the site is read.
        </p>
        <p>
          We collect pages visited, referrer, device type, browser, operating system, language
          and country. The country comes from the approximate location provided by the hosting
          infrastructure or, failing that, from the browser timezone. We also measure a few
          actions on the pages (clicks on outbound links and downloads, article scroll depth,
          copying of code, claps, comments, shares) and a few page-load performance metrics
          (loading time, layout stability and responsiveness). Raw data is kept for 90 days;
          visits for 180 days; beyond that only aggregate totals remain.
        </p>
        <p>
          The browser stores a <code>notrack</code> flag in localStorage only if the
          visitor or the site owner chooses to opt out of being counted: it is a plain
          flag with no identifiers and it is never sent anywhere. The other localStorage entries
          are only preferences (light or dark theme, a game score) and stay on your device.
        </p>

        <hr />
        <h2>2. Data We Collect</h2>
        <p>
          We collect only the necessary data to provide our services:
          Newsletter: If you subscribe, we collect your email address to send
          updates. You can unsubscribe anytime. Comments: We use a self-hosted
          commenting system. Name and email are required to comment; your email
          is never displayed publicly and is only used for communications
          related to your comment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Claps and likes: to prevent double votes we use an identifier derived from your IP
          address and browser (it is never shown and cannot be reversed into the IP). It is a
          pseudonymous datum kept in the database as long as the content stays online, and we
          process it under our legitimate interest in accurate counts.
        </p>
        <hr />

        <h2>3. Third-party Content</h2>
        <p>
          Some articles embed external content: a YouTube video (Google) in "Ligabue e la fine
          della spensieratezza" and a Relive widget in "21 giorni senza alcol". They are not
          loaded until you press "Load the content": until then the provider receives nothing
          from you. After the click the provider receives your IP address and may use cookies
          according to its own policy (for YouTube:
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>).
          Every box also has a link to open the content directly on the provider's site. We do
          not store your choice: the next time you visit, the box is closed again.
        </p>
        <hr />

        <h2>4. Contact Form</h2>
        <p>
          The contact form collects your name, email, message and, if you wish, the type of
          request, so we can reply to you. The message is sent as an email (through the Resend
          service) to my address and is not stored in the site's database. To limit spam we use
          no CAPTCHA and no cookies: your browser solves a small calculation in the
          background, and for a few hours we keep a counter tied to a non-reversible
          fingerprint of your IP address (not the address itself) to stop repeated
          submissions. Legal basis: your request to be contacted and our legitimate interest in
          protecting the form.
        </p>
        <hr />

        <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to: request the deletion of your email from our newsletter;
          request access to, correction or deletion of your comments and the data that goes
          with them; object to processing based on legitimate interest. Write to us at the
          contact below; you may also lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection
          authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).
        </p>
        <hr />

        <h2>6. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy-related inquiries, contact us at: <a
            href="mailto:valerio.narcisi@gmail.com">valerio.narcisi@gmail.com</a
          >
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
